                        "sense_id": "7872cf3d-3f39-386b-8cdb-16eb3adc6d14",
                        "entry_id": "ba32f017-9a66-377a-af2e-be0884410ecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make or be busy; occupy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "rare",
                            "reflexive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35c0a01f-6ce8-4000-8c0a-eb52966e855e",
                                "sense_id": "7872cf3d-3f39-386b-8cdb-16eb3adc6d14",
                                "text": "The whole composition or text is manly, they are not bebusied about Rhetorike flowers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1945df9-babd-4362-93e4-a92a60860949",
                                "sense_id": "7872cf3d-3f39-386b-8cdb-16eb3adc6d14",
                                "text": "There is no time in this month to be spent in idleness. Prudent husbandmen will bebusy and suffer none of their domestics to lounge away their hours as though time was made for sluggards only."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59f45a8d-04af-404e-800d-2a74436d47bf",
                                "sense_id": "7872cf3d-3f39-386b-8cdb-16eb3adc6d14",
                                "text": "To continue: the unrated, as distinguished from the unruly, bebusied themselves with furbishing the barren abodes of Durfee, Farnam and Lawrance."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
